MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me and PTXmas connect my repeated Christmas listening with the a cappella harmonies I associate with The New Old Fashioned.",
    "Stages has some appeal because vocal interpretations interest me, although a cappella Christmas music gives me a stronger reason to choose something now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adele's albums and Django and Jimmie do not offer the combination of holiday songs and vocal harmonies that would motivate me to listen this visit.",
    "Girl-group covers and classic pop harmonies share a vocal connection, but that alone does not make them natural follow-ups to my current interests. Partners gives me too little indication of a match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad interest in singers and vocal albums as enough, when the particular songs and style of singing matter to me.",
    "The list stretches my interest in harmonies toward unrelated pop, country duets, and older hits that I am not currently seeking."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several Christmas interactions in one visit, including returning to The Classic Christmas Album, make familiar holiday music a more concrete interest than general vocal music.",
    "My later interest in The New Old Fashioned adds an a cappella connection, but does not establish that I want Christmas music every visit. This time I would choose just one especially relevant holiday album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in Christmas music and vocal harmonies, but extended it too broadly to vocal albums with little connection to what I want now."
}
